# Normalize line endings to LF for text files on checkout/commit, regardless of a given
# developer's core.autocrlf setting. Windows dev machines here default to core.autocrlf=true
# (see CLAUDE.md's Environment quirks), which was leaving vendor/ blobs with inconsistent line
# endings and causing phantom "modified" status on thousands of files with no real content
# change. eol=lf pins the behavior so it's consistent across Windows dev boxes and the Linux
# hosting/CI side of this project.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit binary declarations as a safety net on top of Git's own content-based detection —
# these must never go through line-ending conversion.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.wav binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.otf binary
*.swf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.z binary
*.ser binary
*.xlsx binary
*.doc binary
*.docx binary
*.p12 binary
*.crt binary
*.fdf binary
*.ai binary
